SIM - 

1. <change shell to csh>
2. source env.cshrc


Part I:
1. cd sim
2. make clean 
3. make compile_verdi
4. Run individual testcases:
  Test 1: ./simv +TEST=full_empty
  Test 2: ./simv +TEST=almost
  Test 3: ./simv +TEST=async_rw
5. Each testcase generates an FSDB file:
  Test 1: test1_full_empty.fsdb
  Test 2: test2_almost.fsdb
  Test 3: test3_async_rw.fsdb
6. Open a testcase waveform in Verdi:
  verdi -dbdir ./simv.daidir -ssf test1_full_empty.fsdb -nologo
  verdi -dbdir ./simv.daidir -ssf test2_almost.fsdb -nologo
  verdi -dbdir ./simv.daidir -ssf test3_async_rw.fsdb -nologo
7. In verdi, add/restore signals in the waveform viewer

Part II:
1. cd sim_odd_even
2. make clean
3. make compile_verdi
4. Run individual testcases:
  Test 1: ./simv +TEST=case4
  Test 2: ./simv +TEST=case5
5. Each testcase generates an FSDB file:
  Test 1: test1_case4.fsdb
  Test 2: test2_case5.fsdb
6. Open a testcase waveform in Verdi:
  verdi -dbdir ./simv.daidir -ssf test1_case4.fsdb -nologo
  verdi -dbdir ./simv.daidir -ssf test2_case5.fsdb -nologo
7. In verdi, add/restore signals in the waveform viewer


SYNTH - 

1. cd synth
2. make -B

